on_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Incident 90c7 comment #10 (read-only diagnosis): '_link_semgrep (scripts/install_review_scanners.py:328-339) does link.symlink_to(semgrep)... A relative symlink target is resolved relative to the symlink's OWN DIRECTORY, so the link... dangles', and the Makefile passes a RELATIVE prefix ($(REVIEW_SCANNER_PREFIX) := .tools/review-scanners).","Same diagnosis: 'pytest NEVER RAN. Execution died inside the install step's own post-install version verification (Makefile:503)... The scanner contracts are untested, not failing.'","Ticket close note: 'The nine SCANNER_INTEGRATION_NODES contracts are UNTESTED, not failing — a materially different starting point for any re-land.'","The plan's Testing/Scope sections instruct to 'Recreate and adapt the reverted tests' but never require a regression test that invokes the installer with a RELATIVE --prefix from a different cwd — the exact gap that let the fault escape."],"finding":"The plan re-lands the reverted scanner artifacts 'as a starting point' without naming or requiring a fix for the relative-prefix / relative-symlink fault that made the original lane die before its contracts ever ran; recreating it verbatim would reproduce the incident's install-step failure.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6c4ef0359a3d737e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope ('Recreate the reverted scanner artifacts from change 2612 as a starting point'); Acceptance Criteria line 'Valid selected scanner locks allow the explicit native-binary target to run the real Semgrep/Gitleaks integration contracts'","norm_id":"n2aa25e7f1d85a2c5","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The advisory lane runs on a real patchset (or on main via the mirror lane), the installer resolves a semgrep symlink under the relative .tools/review-scanners prefix, the link dangles, and the job dies at post-install verification before pytest — leaving the contracts still untested and the ADR-0114 'passing run on main' evidence unattainable."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Scope/Testing, add: 'The recreated installer must resolve the scanner prefix to an absolute path before linking (e.g. _link_semgrep uses semgrep.resolve(), or _selected_prefix returns .resolve()) so a relative Makefile --prefix does not dangle the semgrep symlink; add a RED-first regression test invoking the installer with a relative --prefix from a different working directory that asserts the resulting bin/semgrep is executable and the nine SCANNER_INTEGRATION_NODES contracts run.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["8 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","imp